-names></name><name><surname>Giel</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Harding</surname><given-names>TW</given-names></name><name><surname>Ten horn</surname><given-names>GHMM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ibrahim</surname><given-names>HHA</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Knowledge and Attitudes of Primary Health Care Personnel Concerning Mental Health Problems in Developing Countries: A Follow-Up Study</article-title><source>International Journal of Epidemiology</source><year>1989</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>669</fpage><lpage>673</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2807672</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/ije/18.3.669</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gharaee</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Shariat</surname><given-names>SV</given-names></name><name><surname>Mansouri</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Bolhari</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Yusefi Nouraee</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Rahimi Movaghar</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Case finding in integration of Mental Health Services into Primary Health Care System: Systematic review of the studies conducted in Iran in recent two decades</article-title><source>Iranian Journal of Psychiatry</source><year>2009</year><comment></comment></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kahani</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><source>Effectiveness of mental health training on knowledge, attitude, self care, self esteem and seizure frequency of patients with grand mal epilepsy</source><year>1996</year><publisher-name>Iran University of Medical Science, Tehran Psychiatric Institute</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pezeshki Ghahfarokhi</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Bolhari</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Attitude on mental disorders in inhabitants of some villages of North of Tehran</article-title><source>Iranian Journal of Psychiatry and Clinical Psychology</source><year>1995</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>68</fpage><lpage>75</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Abhari</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A descriptive report on mental health services and integration of mental health in primary health care in Savojbolagh</article-title><source>Iranian Journal of Psychiatry and Clinical Psychology</source><year>1999</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>29</fpage><lpage>39</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bakhshani</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Bolhari</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bayan zadeh</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Promoting community based mental health</article-title><source>Iranian Journal of Psychiatry and Clinical Psychology</source><year>2000</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>53</fpage><lpage>61</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Malekafzali</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of helath programs of the country in the past and present, and suggestions for future programs</article-title><source>Hakim</source><year>1999</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>63</fpage><lpage>66</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group pe